Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: give the clustered scene shader a no-subgroups path

With 0023-0025 in, Forward+ still drew nothing, and the reason was not a
validation error at all:

  1234x ERROR: Parameter "current_cluster_builder" is null.
              at: _render_scene (render_forward_clustered.cpp:1770)
    18x ERROR: Tint SPIR-V->WGSL failed: 'subgroupOr' must only be called from
              subgroup uniform control flow
    18x ERROR: WebGPU: SPIR-V->WGSL conversion failed for stage 1.

Patch 0015 gave cluster_render.glsl an explicit no-subgroups variant and taught
the cluster builder to honour LIMIT_SUBGROUP_*. It did not touch
scene_forward_clustered.glsl, which calls subgroupMin, subgroupMax, subgroupOr
and subgroupBroadcastFirst with no #ifdef of any kind, and whose include
enables the subgroup extensions unconditionally. WebGPU exposes no subgroup
support, so the scene shader failed translation, so no cluster builder was ever
created, so _render_scene returned early on every single frame.

The reductions are a divergence optimisation, not a correctness requirement.
subgroupBroadcastFirst(subgroupMin(item_from)) makes every lane in a subgroup
walk the same cluster item range so the loop branches coherently; each lane
already holds its own correct item_from, item_to and mask. Defining the four
reductions as identity therefore gathers exactly the same lights, decals and
reflection probes, with less coherent branching -- the same argument 0015
recorded for the cluster builder's atomicOr fallback.

Rather than guard ten call sites, the fallback is four identity macros in
scene_forward_clustered_inc.glsl behind #ifdef USE_SUBGROUPS, and
render_forward_clustered.cpp now defines USE_SUBGROUPS only when the device
reports ballot + arithmetic subgroup ops in the fragment stage -- the same test
cluster_builder_rd.cpp already applies.

diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered_inc.glsl b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered_inc.glsl
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered_inc.glsl
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/shaders/forward_clustered/scene_forward_clustered_inc.glsl
@@ -5,8 +5,32 @@
 #define MAX_VOXEL_GI_INSTANCES 8
 #define MAX_VIEWS 2
 
+// The clustered scene shader uses subgroup reductions to make every lane in a
+// subgroup walk the SAME cluster item range, so the loop below branches
+// coherently. It is a divergence optimisation, not a correctness requirement:
+// each lane already holds its own correct item_from/item_to and its own mask.
+//
+// WebGPU exposes subgroups only as an optional feature (Chrome 134+), so no
+// portable baseline may assume them, and this build does not request them.
+// Unlike the cluster builder --
+// which patch 0015 gave an explicit no-subgroups variant -- these call sites had
+// no guard whatsoever, so Tint rejected the whole scene shader with
+// "subgroupOr must only be called from subgroup uniform control flow". A scene
+// shader that does not translate means no cluster builder, which means
+// _render_scene returns early and Forward+ never draws anything.
+//
+// Defining the reductions as identity leaves each lane using its own value:
+// the same lights, decals and reflections are gathered, just with less coherent
+// branching. Correct everywhere, optimal only where subgroups exist.
+#ifdef USE_SUBGROUPS
 #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_ballot : enable
 #extension GL_KHR_shader_subgroup_arithmetic : enable
+#else
+#define subgroupBroadcastFirst(m_value) (m_value)
+#define subgroupMin(m_value) (m_value)
+#define subgroupMax(m_value) (m_value)
+#define subgroupOr(m_value) (m_value)
+#endif
 
 #include "../cluster_data_inc.glsl"
 #include "../decal_data_inc.glsl"
diff --git a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp
--- a/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp
+++ b/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp
@@ -5147,6 +5147,24 @@
 		}
 #endif
 
+		{
+			// Match the cluster builder's rule (cluster_builder_rd.cpp): the scene
+			// shader's subgroup reductions may only be compiled in when the device
+			// actually exposes ballot + arithmetic subgroup ops in the fragment
+			// stage. WebGPU exposes none, and emitting them anyway fails shader
+			// translation outright rather than degrading.
+			RenderingDevice *rd = RD::get_singleton();
+			const uint64_t subgroup_stages = rd->limit_get(RD::LIMIT_SUBGROUP_IN_SHADERS);
+			const uint64_t subgroup_ops = rd->limit_get(RD::LIMIT_SUBGROUP_OPERATIONS);
+			const bool subgroups_usable =
+					(subgroup_stages & RD::SHADER_STAGE_FRAGMENT_BIT) &&
+					(subgroup_ops & RD::SUBGROUP_BALLOT_BIT) &&
+					(subgroup_ops & RD::SUBGROUP_ARITHMETIC_BIT);
+			if (subgroups_usable) {
+				defines += "\n#define USE_SUBGROUPS\n";
+			}
+		}
+
 		scene_shader.init(defines);
 	}
 
